Subject: [PATCH] ao_coreaudio: clear AudioUnit after failed initialization cleanup

init_audiounit() disposes its component on failure. The outer init() error
path now calls uninit(), so leaving the disposed handle in priv causes Stop,
Uninitialize and Dispose to be called on that stale handle a second time.
Clear it after disposal so the outer partial-initialization cleanup skips it.

This local follow-up applies after mpv-0.41.0-coreaudio-init-failure.patch.

diff --git a/audio/out/ao_coreaudio.c b/audio/out/ao_coreaudio.c
--- a/audio/out/ao_coreaudio.c
+++ b/audio/out/ao_coreaudio.c
@@ -349,6 +349,7 @@ coreaudio_error_audiounit:
     AudioUnitUninitialize(p->audio_unit);
 coreaudio_error_component:
     AudioComponentInstanceDispose(p->audio_unit);
+    p->audio_unit = NULL;
 coreaudio_error:
     return false;
 }
